# Platform capability conditions must gate upstream CTest registration
id:                     E7003-draft-2301_80739235
trigger_tool:           cmake|ctest|conan-create|clang
phase:                  configure|build|test
error_signature:        "no type named 'suspend_point'|no member named 'suspend'|__TBB_RESUMABLE_TASKS"
severity:               2
category:               cmake|platform-capability|upstream-tests
match_keywords:         target capability macro, platform-conditional CTest inventory, unsupported upstream test registration, OHOS non-glibc
root_cause:             An upstream CMake test list can register a test unconditionally even when the test source excludes itself or its public API is disabled by a target capability macro. On OHOS oneTBB sets __TBB_RESUMABLE_TASKS false because the target is Linux-like but not glibc, while the resumable-task conformance target still compiles against the unavailable API.
affected_scope:         Cross-built CMake projects whose test registration is broader than the target platform capability set.
verification_cmd:       Enable the upstream test option, inspect the target capability macro and registration site, apply the smallest platform condition, then run the complete remaining CTest inventory and record the excluded test name and reason.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           capability-gated-test-registration
rec_description:        Keep the upstream test option enabled. Gate only the unsupported target using the exact CMake platform or capability condition, preserve every other test, and report source inventory and target-supported inventory as separate denominators.
rec_command:            "inspect capability macro and test/CMakeLists.txt; patch one registration; run ctest --output-on-failure"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               test-registration
fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      source-guard-only
fallback_description:   A source-level empty translation unit is insufficient because it can leave a no-op CTest target counted as passed. Use a CMake registration gate when the test cannot exist on the target.
fallback_command:       "do not count an empty unsupported test target; preserve an explicit exclusion record"
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          ctest-inventory
forbid_1_pattern:       "TBB_TEST.*OFF|disable.*all.*tests"
forbid_1_reason:        Disabling the complete upstream suite hides supported tests and invalidates the coverage denominator.
forbid_1_consequence:   The CI result cannot prove the target test inventory.
forbid_2_pattern:       "empty.*translation unit|no-op.*CTest"
forbid_2_reason:        A buildable no-op target is not evidence that the unsupported API works.
forbid_2_consequence:   CI can report a false pass while executing no test cases.
principles:             P007, P015
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to:
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
